course: dictionary
lesson: 7309
title: Words that turn: pivot
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pivot is the fixed point that something turns around. «A seesaw is a lever with the pivot in the middle, so a child sitting far out can lift a grown-up sitting close in.» The pivot stays still while the seesaw moves.
explain: Pivot can also be a verb. To pivot means to turn around on one point. In basketball and netball, a player keeps one foot still and turns on it. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Pivot can also mean the most important part that everything else depends on, or a change of plan. «"Pivot" often means a change of plan because the first plan failed.» Look at the words around the word to find out which meaning fits.
fact: A pivot is the fixed point or pin on which something turns or balances.
fact: To pivot means to turn around on one point.
fact: In a lever, the pivot is also called the fulcrum.
fact: A light child far from the pivot can balance a heavy child close to it.
fact: «A pivot joint at the top of the neck» lets you turn your head to shake it «no».
exercise: «A seesaw is a lever with the pivot in the middle.» What is the pivot on a seesaw? | *The point in the middle that it turns on | The handle at the top | The seat at the far end | The ground under the child's feet
exercise: In basketball, Sam keeps one foot still and turns on it. What is this called? | Running fast | Dribbling | Shooting a hoop | *Pivoting
exercise: «"Pivot" often means a change of plan because the first plan failed.» What does pivot mean here? | A hard shout | *A change of plan | A rule that never changes | A small wooden stick
test: «A pivot joint at the top of your neck lets you shake your head.» What movement does this joint allow? | Clapping your hands | Bending your knee | Opening a jar | *Turning your head from side to side
test: Which meaning of pivot fits this sentence: «The plan pivots on one thing: the first person who arrives.» | Turns around in a circle | Makes a loud noise | *Depends mostly on one key thing | Moves very quickly
exam: Ella says, «The whole game pivots on our goalkeeper.» What does pivots mean here? | Runs away from the game | Sleeps during the game | Changes the colour of the team shirts | *Depends mostly on one key thing
